`pragma protect end_protected
// When start is asserted, sequence begins. Sequence always begins in alignment phase
// Alignment phase: Works according to the below:
// Gen1/2: If FTS, sends 4 EIEs, then sends FTS's, if TS1, sends EIEOS, then pretend TS1's
// Gen3+ Sends an EIEOS, then FTS's with periodic EIEOS's.
// If align_len is 0, remains in align phase until data_en is asserted, otherwise sends align_len FTS's / pretend TS1's.
// When switching from alignment phase to data phase, a SDP (gen1/2) or a SDS (gen3+) is sent. This tells the checker to switch to the data phase.
// Data phase: Sends data pattern. If data_len is set, runs that number of blocks, sends an EIOSQ, transitions to electrical idle, and asserts done.
// If data_len is not set, runs continuously until start is deasserted. Then an EIOSQ is sent and transitions to electrical idle. Done is not asserted.
// In all phases, every align_spacing number of blocks one or more SKP OS's is inserted
//

// Note: For Gen1/2, data_len is in terms of data blocks (8b), but this actually means "scheduled". Generator will not insert a SKP inside an FTS
// or a TS1, and will only insert a SKP every clock (20b or 40b). ie. inserts if possible and counter >= maximum

// Note: Spec says SKP OS's should not be sent during N_FTS, and one immediately following FTS's for extended sync, and is not explicitly done here.

